1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:02,700
=EP01 Behind-the-Scenes=

2
00:00:02,780 --> 00:00:05,980
(Behind-the Scenes 1)

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:08,100
(Behind-the Scenes)

4
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:09,710
What do you think is nice in Tianjin?

5
00:00:11,510 --> 00:00:11,990
Carbs.

6
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:14,430
Carbs?

7
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:17,950
There's just lots of breakfast.

8
00:00:17,950 --> 00:00:19,140
Yesterday, Wu Siying

9
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:20,400
ate jianbing guozi.

10
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,350
The buldak ramen one?

11
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:22,190
Yeah.

12
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,310
Is it a Tianjin delicacy?

13
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,190
It is,

14
00:00:26,190 --> 00:00:28,620
but there are many variety now.

15
00:00:29,760 --> 00:00:31,070
The most authentic one
is the classic kind

16
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:33,270
with a guozi,

17
00:00:33,280 --> 00:00:34,390
that crispy cracker.

18
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:37,310
Tianjin's most iconic dish

19
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,580
is probably Eight Treasure tofu.

20
00:00:39,060 --> 00:00:40,270
Eight Treasure tofu?

21
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:41,180
(Repeats)
Yes.

22
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:44,670
The tofu has a crispy crust
on the outside,

23
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:46,110
but it's also kind of sweet.

24
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:49,590
It's more savory. Sweet and savory.

25
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:51,470
Yeah. We could make Tianjin dishes.

26
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:54,230
Serve them in Northeast China portions,

27
00:00:54,240 --> 00:00:55,550
so everyone can eat.

28
00:00:56,280 --> 00:00:57,470
We're in an assembly line.

29
00:00:57,480 --> 00:00:59,110
Yeah. No problem.

30
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:01,900
Tianjin.

31
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:03,150
Tianjin, yes.

32
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:06,790
How do you introduce yourself
in Tianjin dialect?

33
00:01:07,020 --> 00:01:07,860
(Glances)

34
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:09,060
(Excited)

35
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:10,710
He'll go first.

36
00:01:10,720 --> 00:01:12,270
He's raring to go.

37
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,670
No. I'm just waiting for you to say it.

38
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:15,740
(Laughs)

39
00:01:15,800 --> 00:01:17,350
I've never tried saying my name

40
00:01:17,360 --> 00:01:18,190
in Tianjin dialect.

41
00:01:18,600 --> 00:01:19,380
It's not that I'm shy.

42
00:01:19,380 --> 00:01:20,870
I just don't know how.

43
00:01:20,870 --> 00:01:21,400
Yeah.

44
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:23,230
We don't normally speak
in Tianjin dialect.

45
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:23,880
Yeah.

46
00:01:23,880 --> 00:01:25,830
We need the right environment
to pick it up.

47
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:28,270
Probably need to hear the birds singing.

48
00:01:30,260 --> 00:01:35,180
(Behind-the-Scenes 2)

49
00:01:35,220 --> 00:01:35,920
(Behind-the-Scenes)

50
00:01:35,920 --> 00:01:38,030
(Asks)
What do you usually listen to?

51
00:01:38,030 --> 00:01:38,660
Music?

52
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:39,560
Yea. Singer.

53
00:01:39,560 --> 00:01:40,630
I want to know

54
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,110
if you have any singer you like.

55
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:43,390
G.E.M.

56
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:44,470
And Jackson Wang.

57
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,060
As for me...

58
00:01:49,060 --> 00:01:49,950
Lately,

59
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:51,730
I've been listening

60
00:01:51,730 --> 00:01:52,520
to Dou Jingtong.

61
00:01:54,760 --> 00:01:55,750
What about Cui Yihang?

62
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:57,460
Your turn.

63
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,020
Me first?

64
00:01:58,020 --> 00:01:58,830
You first.

65
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:01,850
Eric Chou.

66
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:02,670
Do you all know him?

67
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:09,900
(High-five)

68
00:02:11,040 --> 00:02:11,690
What is it?

69
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:12,920
I was about to say Eric Chou too.

70
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:13,830
I like him a lot too.

71
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:14,780
(Surprised)
Really.

72
00:02:16,170 --> 00:02:16,780
Not only...

73
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:18,470
We have such good chemistry.

74
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:24,430
Sorry, I just...

75
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,230
Let me ask your name again.

76
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,220
Sun Bohan.

77
00:02:28,220 --> 00:02:29,070
Wood and white for Bo.

78
00:02:29,400 --> 00:02:29,870
Cultured for Han.

79
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:30,590
Sun Bohan.

80
00:02:30,590 --> 00:02:31,050
Yes.

81
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,660
(Raises hand)
Yu Yang.

82
00:02:32,910 --> 00:02:33,270
Yu Yang.

83
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:34,010
I know.

84
00:02:34,010 --> 00:02:34,290
Yeah.

85
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:35,790
He doesn't need to tell me.

86
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:37,530
Heyun.

87
00:02:37,910 --> 00:02:38,740
Heyun.

88
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:39,780
(Yes)
Yes, Heyun.

89
00:02:39,900 --> 00:02:40,630
Heyun?

90
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:41,290
It's Chen Hewen.

91
00:02:41,510 --> 00:02:42,260
Chen Hewen, oh yes.

92
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:43,110
(Scratches head)
Chen Hewen.

93
00:02:43,410 --> 00:02:44,210
I even said yes.

94
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:45,470
You even said yes.

95
00:02:45,600 --> 00:02:47,310
Weren't we just best friends?

96
00:02:47,310 --> 00:02:47,840
What happened?

97
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,270
I'm sorry.

98
00:02:52,040 --> 00:02:53,240
You wouldn't pick him, would you?

99
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,260
You won't vote for him, right?

100
00:02:56,520 --> 00:02:57,830
I was actually thinking about it.

101
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,430
I thought about it yesterday too.

102
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,430
Congrats, you two found your match.

103
00:03:01,430 --> 00:03:02,780
(Teasing)

104
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:11,220
(Behind-the-Scenes 3)

105
00:03:11,580 --> 00:03:13,940
(First dinner together)

106
00:03:13,940 --> 00:03:14,420
(Behind-the-Scenes)

107
00:03:14,420 --> 00:03:15,500
(Glances)

108
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:17,550
W...

109
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,270
What's your hobby again?

110
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:21,070
Playing piano.

111
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:23,310
What did you major in?

112
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,550
Music therapy.

113
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:26,590
(Music therapy)
Have you heard of it?

114
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,830
Music therapy?

115
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:29,630
Yes.

116
00:03:31,120 --> 00:03:31,910
Music therapy?

117
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:32,990
You've heard of it?

118
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,820
Yes.

119
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:35,820
(Glances)

120
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:37,790
At my school,

121
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:39,230
at the entrance,

122
00:03:39,240 --> 00:03:40,670
there are often

123
00:03:40,680 --> 00:03:41,750
music therapy students

124
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,470
sitting in a circle

125
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:43,990
playing drums together.

126
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:46,110
They play all morning.

127
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:47,030
I don't know...

128
00:03:47,040 --> 00:03:47,910
Yeah, it's a drum circle.

129
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:49,870
Is it

130
00:03:49,880 --> 00:03:51,060
that disc?

131
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:51,940
(Curious)

132
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:52,750
No.

133
00:03:52,760 --> 00:03:54,000
It's more like

134
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:55,000
African drums.

135
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:55,380
Yes.

136
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:56,020
(Understands)

137
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:56,590
Yeah.

138
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,270
Did you study music?

139
00:03:58,280 --> 00:03:59,350
I studied

140
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:00,190
traditional music.

141
00:04:00,310 --> 00:04:00,920
I play the flute.

142
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:02,950
We could start a band.

143
00:04:02,960 --> 00:04:03,910
(Suggestion)
I like singing.

144
00:04:05,440 --> 00:04:07,390
I just like to sing.

145
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,270
I'll handle production.

146
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:11,670
Okay.

147
00:04:12,560 --> 00:04:13,270
Sure.

148
00:04:14,340 --> 00:04:15,140
We've got our keyboard player.

149
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:16,540
(Loves playing piano)

150
00:04:16,690 --> 00:04:17,750
We have...

151
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:19,550
I can sing and dance.

152
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,390
Either is fine.

153
00:04:32,100 --> 00:04:37,020
(Behind-the-Scenes 4)

154
00:04:37,060 --> 00:04:39,060
(Behind-the-Scenes)

155
00:04:39,080 --> 00:04:41,790
Let's go.

156
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:43,310
Let's leave this here first.

157
00:04:43,310 --> 00:04:43,930
Sure.

158
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:44,590
It'll be fine.

159
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,230
Okay.

160
00:04:46,520 --> 00:04:47,300
Have a seat.

161
00:04:47,300 --> 00:04:47,790
Take a seat.

162
00:04:48,440 --> 00:04:49,830
Grab a notebook.

163
00:04:50,400 --> 00:04:52,190
Should we write our names first?

164
00:04:53,180 --> 00:04:54,190
I'll sit here.

165
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:54,950
Okay.

166
00:04:55,130 --> 00:04:55,890
Write down

167
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,790
what we said.

168
00:04:58,200 --> 00:04:59,390
Yeah. Make a note.

169
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:02,380
It'll be easier to get to know everyone.

170
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:03,140
(Records everyone's info)

171
00:05:03,320 --> 00:05:05,710
I'll write about you on the first page.

172
00:05:05,710 --> 00:05:06,540
(Asking Zhao Xilun)

173
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,710
Wish for Xi, right?

174
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:08,870
Yes.

175
00:05:08,880 --> 00:05:09,750
(Name)
Relationship for Lun.

176
00:05:11,360 --> 00:05:12,350
Okay.

177
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:13,990
Are you gonna have one page
for each person?

178
00:05:15,160 --> 00:05:16,950
I'll do this before I sleep.

179
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:18,070
Let's head out then.

180
00:05:18,070 --> 00:05:18,540
Okay.

181
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,270
I'll write whoever I see first.

182
00:05:22,320 --> 00:05:23,190
Wu Siying, what is yours?

183
00:05:23,190 --> 00:05:24,310
(Asks Wu Siying)
What's your MBTI?

184
00:05:24,320 --> 00:05:25,270
I'll write it down.

185
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:26,340
INFP (the Mediator).

186
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:27,150
INFP (the Mediator).

187
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:28,070
Liang Renfang is

188
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:29,230
(Asks Liang Renfang)
ENFP.

189
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:30,030
Yes.

190
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:30,910
ENFP (the Campaigner).

191
00:05:31,360 --> 00:05:32,670
(Serious)
You can write a yearbook.

192
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:33,590
Yeah.

193
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:34,870
Sun Qimeng.

194
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:36,270
(Asks Sun Qimeng)
Can I get some of your details?

195
00:05:36,280 --> 00:05:36,880
Please?

196
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:37,540
Sure.

197
00:05:37,760 --> 00:05:38,630
Ask away.

198
00:05:38,640 --> 00:05:39,470
What do you want to know?

199
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:40,600
(Birthday)
When were you born?

200
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:41,750
4 September.

201
00:05:42,040 --> 00:05:43,030
(Hometown)
Where are you from?

202
00:05:43,040 --> 00:05:44,190
I'm from Shandong.

203
00:05:44,250 --> 00:05:44,830
Shandong.

204
00:05:45,020 --> 00:05:45,550
Okay.

205
00:05:46,210 --> 00:05:47,790
When I learn about other things
about you,

206
00:05:47,800 --> 00:05:48,910
I'll write them down myself.

207
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:50,310
You'll have recorded lots of stuff.

208
00:05:50,320 --> 00:05:52,310
(Joking)
I'll bring them with me everywhere.

209
00:05:52,760 --> 00:05:54,080
(Asks Cao Yiheng)
Exercise...

210
00:05:54,490 --> 00:05:55,810
(Hobby)
Exercise?

211
00:05:55,810 --> 00:05:56,490
Pool.

212
00:05:57,090 --> 00:05:57,720
Oh, pool.

213
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:58,950
Since you're here,

214
00:05:58,960 --> 00:06:00,870
help me complete the notes.

215
00:06:00,880 --> 00:06:03,540
(Asks Yu Yang)
I've recorded what I already know.

216
00:06:03,920 --> 00:06:04,710
Yu of yu shi.
[*yu shi = therefore]

217
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:06,310
This one.

218
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:08,270
Yang of hai yang.
[*hai yang = the ocean]

219
00:06:08,980 --> 00:06:09,360
Yes.

220
00:06:10,030 --> 00:06:10,670
And then...

221
00:06:11,600 --> 00:06:12,510
Your age.

222
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:13,310
1995.

223
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:14,920
1995 and...

224
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:15,360
March.

225
00:06:16,110 --> 00:06:16,750
March...

226
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,430
My writing is so bad.

227
00:06:19,610 --> 00:06:21,260
Do you think me questioning you

228
00:06:21,280 --> 00:06:22,430
makes me look serious?

229
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:23,930
Not really.

230
00:06:23,930 --> 00:06:24,280
Okay.

231
00:06:24,280 --> 00:06:25,070
Very detailed.

232
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:31,820
(Behind-the-Scenes 5)

233
00:06:31,860 --> 00:06:33,860
(Behind-the-Scenes)

234
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:34,980
(Glances)

235
00:06:36,760 --> 00:06:37,790
I think if I stare a bit more,

236
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:39,590
my contacts might fall out.

237
00:06:39,590 --> 00:06:40,300
It might slip out.

238
00:06:40,320 --> 00:06:42,150
Go take it out.

239
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:45,430
I think I can go change into my glasses.

240
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,140
Then switch to your regular glasses
and come back.

241
00:06:48,340 --> 00:06:50,140
(Turns around)

242
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:52,110
Should we go downstairs?

243
00:06:52,120 --> 00:06:54,230
Yeah, let's take a look.

244
00:06:54,840 --> 00:06:55,910
When Cao Yiheng comes back later,

245
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:57,420
he'll find this place empty.

246
00:06:57,420 --> 00:06:59,420
(Smiles)

247
00:06:59,480 --> 00:07:01,030
Everyone's missing.

248
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:01,670
Yesh.

249
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,590
Right, where did he go?

250
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:04,870
He went to change his glasses.

251
00:07:10,060 --> 00:07:11,340
(Glancing around)

252
00:07:17,960 --> 00:07:18,750
You took them out?

253
00:07:20,080 --> 00:07:21,590
Yes. I realized
they didn't really match.

254
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:22,910
What kind of frame?

255
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,110
But I can show you.

256
00:07:24,170 --> 00:07:24,690
Sure.

257
00:07:24,840 --> 00:07:26,620
Did you go outside
and realize we were gone?

258
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,270
Did you go?

259
00:07:27,280 --> 00:07:28,310
Did you hear us coming down?

260
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:29,230
I heard you.

261
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:32,470
It looks like this.

262
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:35,380
(Checking out)

263
00:07:35,480 --> 00:07:36,550
Not bad.

264
00:07:38,240 --> 00:07:40,030
You look really smart.

265
00:07:40,320 --> 00:07:41,980
Look very smart.

266
00:07:41,980 --> 00:07:42,660
(Laughs)

267
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:48,940
(Behind-the-Scenes 6)

268
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:50,790
((Behind-the-Scenes)
I kinda want to eat supper.

269
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,270
How about we make something?

270
00:07:52,650 --> 00:07:53,570
Wash the pot first.

271
00:07:54,320 --> 00:07:56,910
Rinse it with hot water.
There's some over there.

272
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,470
This feels like it was washed.

273
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:00,870
Has this been washed?

274
00:08:01,500 --> 00:08:02,820
(Looks up)

275
00:08:02,840 --> 00:08:04,070
Is this the noodle we're using?

276
00:08:04,220 --> 00:08:05,060
(Walks over)

277
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:06,670
Are we just having noodles?

278
00:08:08,040 --> 00:08:09,390
Sorry for troubling you guys.

279
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:10,380
It's alright.

280
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,230
I was just thinking

281
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,230
if I can put that mapo tofu

282
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,110
on top of the noodles.

283
00:08:13,960 --> 00:08:15,110
I think you two...

284
00:08:16,760 --> 00:08:18,110
(Comes closer)
After putting on the apron,

285
00:08:18,320 --> 00:08:19,940
you look like you're on a cooking show.

286
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:21,860
(Cooking competition)

287
00:08:21,880 --> 00:08:22,990
Should we add tomatoes?

288
00:08:22,990 --> 00:08:24,390
I can cut them.

289
00:08:24,390 --> 00:08:25,230
Blanch them first.

290
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:26,070
Sure.

291
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:26,770
Make it healthier.

292
00:08:28,060 --> 00:08:29,020
(Comes over to help)

293
00:08:29,880 --> 00:08:31,790
(Asks)
Sha Yue'er, do you want tomatoes?

294
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:34,100
(Glances)

295
00:08:34,500 --> 00:08:34,950
No.

296
00:08:35,790 --> 00:08:36,670
You don't like tomatoes.

297
00:08:36,930 --> 00:08:37,700
Hang on.

298
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:38,830
The main issue is

299
00:08:38,840 --> 00:08:40,190
that this is pork bone broth noodles,

300
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,310
Tomatoes don't really go with it.

301
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:43,010
(Changes his mind)
Yeah, tomatoes would be a little...

302
00:08:43,120 --> 00:08:44,150
If you add tomatoes...

303
00:08:44,610 --> 00:08:47,730
Maybe something
like pickled vegetables would work.

304
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:48,870
I forgot.

305
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:49,750
This is

306
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,270
pork bone broth. I failed as a cook.

307
00:08:52,280 --> 00:08:52,790
My bad.

308
00:08:53,160 --> 00:08:54,110
(Comforts)
It's fine.

309
00:08:54,120 --> 00:08:55,660
It's not nearly that serious.

310
00:08:55,940 --> 00:08:57,060
(Glances)

311
00:09:04,300 --> 00:09:05,940
(Sushi is heated)

312
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:08,990
Anyone want some?

313
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,030
I'll get you some chopsticks.

314
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:11,580
What's this?

315
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:12,520
Sushi.

316
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,240
Foie gras sushi.

317
00:09:13,390 --> 00:09:14,560
I want some.

318
00:09:15,040 --> 00:09:16,550
Here, then.

319
00:09:16,880 --> 00:09:17,350
Thank you.

320
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,380
(Hands it over)

321
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:20,830
Put it here first.

322
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,510
I just heated it. Give it a try.

323
00:09:22,680 --> 00:09:23,190
Okay.

324
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:30,870
It's quite nice.

325
00:09:31,220 --> 00:09:36,140
(Behind-the-Scenes 7)

326
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:38,180
(Behind-the-Scenes)

327
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:39,310
Do you like watching movies?

328
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:40,350
Yes.

329
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:41,910
What have you watched recently?

330
00:09:41,920 --> 00:09:43,510
Or what's your favorite movie?

331
00:09:45,120 --> 00:09:45,950
What do you like?

332
00:09:45,950 --> 00:09:46,580
(Questions in return)

333
00:09:47,160 --> 00:09:47,950
"Interstellar"

334
00:09:49,440 --> 00:09:51,210
I cry every time I talk about it.

335
00:09:51,280 --> 00:09:51,630
Really?

336
00:09:51,640 --> 00:09:53,030
I cry every time I watch it.

337
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,310
I'm a little sentimental.

338
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:55,110
Because, at its core...

339
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:57,110
(Listens intently)
It's pretty hardcore sci-fi,

340
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,910
but at its heart, it's about love.

341
00:10:00,520 --> 00:10:02,070
Yeah. I think you should watch it.

342
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:03,790
What kind of movies do you like?

343
00:10:07,120 --> 00:10:08,070
I like mysteries.

344
00:10:08,080 --> 00:10:10,230
I feel like I've watched
almost every mystery movie there is.

345
00:10:10,880 --> 00:10:11,670
For example?

346
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:13,630
"Murder on the Orient Express"

347
00:10:13,640 --> 00:10:14,750
"Witness for the Prosecution"

348
00:10:15,120 --> 00:10:15,790
"Witness for the Prosecution"?

349
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:16,710
Have you seen it?

350
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,830
I usually watch recap videos
for mystery movies.

351
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:21,910
(Laughs)
I rarely watch the actual movie.

352
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,070
Actually,

353
00:10:25,280 --> 00:10:26,670
when I'm really upset,

354
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:28,070
I might watch something

355
00:10:28,120 --> 00:10:29,390
like astronomy

356
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:30,710
or physics

357
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:31,790
because I feel like

358
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:33,590
it gives me a sense of vastness
of existence.

359
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:34,610
Yes.

360
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:35,120
Right?

361
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:36,240
(I get it)
I understand.

362
00:10:36,360 --> 00:10:38,270
History and astronomy
are essentially the same.

363
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:39,230
A sense of vastness of existence.

364
00:10:39,800 --> 00:10:40,770
Physics too.

365
00:10:41,270 --> 00:10:42,170
Yes, physics does that too.

366
00:10:42,320 --> 00:10:43,450
I almost

367
00:10:43,450 --> 00:10:44,700
chose physics as my major.

368
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:48,110
I actually regret not choosing physics.

369
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:50,910
But it's really difficult
and exhausting.

370
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:52,070
It is.

371
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:53,950
But I think studying physics

372
00:10:53,950 --> 00:10:56,560
allows one to understand
the world better.

373
00:10:56,560 --> 00:10:56,960
Yes.

374
00:10:57,040 --> 00:10:57,710
I think

375
00:10:57,920 --> 00:10:58,550
the fundamental sciences

376
00:10:58,560 --> 00:11:00,470
are the true laws governing
how the world works.

377
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:01,350
I agree.

378
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,230
Human civilization is just

379
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:04,550
so insignificant.

380
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:10,740
(Behind-the-Scenes 8)

381
00:11:10,820 --> 00:11:12,140
(Behind-the-Scenes: Signal House)

382
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,070
We can play pool.

383
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:13,950
Sure.

384
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:16,980
Nice shot.

385
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:22,370
Great shot.

386
00:11:22,710 --> 00:11:23,290
Your turn.

387
00:11:26,020 --> 00:11:27,340
(Turns to look)

388
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:28,870
Do you know how to play pool?

389
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:29,890
I hit it randomly.

390
00:11:30,080 --> 00:11:31,240
I'm not very good.

391
00:11:31,800 --> 00:11:33,390
I don't know how to play at all.

392
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:34,870
Just hit it.

393
00:11:37,200 --> 00:11:37,960
Do you want to play?

394
00:11:37,960 --> 00:11:38,910
Do you know how?

395
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:39,950
Want to give it a go?

396
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,150
(Recommends)
She can play.

397
00:11:41,840 --> 00:11:42,510
You know how to play?

398
00:11:43,200 --> 00:11:44,150
I just hit them.

399
00:11:44,560 --> 00:11:45,670
It's fine. It's hard to play.

400
00:11:48,720 --> 00:11:49,830
Looks professional

401
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:51,060
(Expectant)

402
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:53,620
(Misses)

403
00:11:56,970 --> 00:11:57,930
This...

404
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:01,310
Start over.

405
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,510
Get a feel of the ball first.

406
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:03,990
Feel the friction.

407
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:05,820
Okay.

408
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:07,950
This is so embarrassing.
Quick. Who wants to play?

409
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:08,630
Come play.

410
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,310
I've learned it before,

411
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,790
but I can never hit the ball.

412
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:13,510
How do I position my hand?

413
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:14,870
Like this.

414
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:15,950
Teach me.

415
00:12:16,160 --> 00:12:17,070
(Teaching)
Put your hand here.

416
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,550
Make a heart with it.

417
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:20,550
Keep your hand level with the cue.

418
00:12:20,560 --> 00:12:21,670
Look here.

419
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:23,030
Then just...

420
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:24,500
(Makes the shot)

421
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:25,390
Nice.

422
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:25,910
Talented.

423
00:12:26,160 --> 00:12:26,790
You're really good.

424
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:27,710
You got it right away.

425
00:12:27,920 --> 00:12:28,830
She's a good teacher.

426
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:29,790
I just said stuff.

427
00:12:31,380 --> 00:12:36,300
(Behind-the-Scenes 9)

428
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:36,780
(Behind-the-Scenes)

429
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:37,670
What do you want to make?

430
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:41,510
Stir-fried beef with scrambled eggs
and tomatoes.

431
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,350
(Repeats)
Stir-fried beef with scrambled eggs

432
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:44,870
and tomatoes.

433
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:47,780
It's basically a rice bowl.

434
00:12:47,780 --> 00:12:48,220
(Glances)

435
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:50,350
Can't wait.

436
00:12:50,560 --> 00:12:51,550
Okay.

437
00:12:54,080 --> 00:12:54,910
I'm cooking rice.

438
00:12:56,760 --> 00:12:59,300
The container we washed earlier...

439
00:12:59,460 --> 00:13:00,260
(Gets up immediately)

440
00:13:00,280 --> 00:13:00,790
It's here.

441
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:04,580
Alright.

442
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:06,020
(Hands it over)

443
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:07,590
Thanks.

444
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:10,070
For five people...

445
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:10,710
Five cups.

446
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:11,910
That should be about right.

447
00:13:12,760 --> 00:13:13,710
Let's just go by that.

448
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:16,740
(Helps)

449
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:18,990
We can eat something else
if it's not enough.

450
00:13:18,990 --> 00:13:19,580
Yeah.

451
00:13:25,480 --> 00:13:26,190
Done.

452
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:27,430
Alright.

453
00:13:28,800 --> 00:13:29,110
Here.

454
00:13:29,660 --> 00:13:30,260
Wipe it a bit.

455
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:30,870
Have to wipe it.

456
00:13:30,870 --> 00:13:31,220
Yes.

457
00:13:31,220 --> 00:13:33,820
(Grabs tissue)

458
00:13:37,240 --> 00:13:38,500
Your hands.

459
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:40,260
(Swap sides)

460
00:13:42,660 --> 00:13:43,940
(Glances)

461
00:13:43,960 --> 00:13:45,070
Okay.

462
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,230
We don't need this. I'll put it away.

463
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:58,140
(Cleaning up)

464
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:01,740
(Throws)

465
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:06,270
We're done.

466
00:14:06,280 --> 00:14:07,190
So quick.

467
00:14:07,560 --> 00:14:08,910
Tasting session.

468
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:09,820
Well.

469
00:14:10,960 --> 00:14:11,470
Okay.

470
00:14:12,160 --> 00:14:12,670
Is it nice?

471
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:13,510
I'll grab a bite.

472
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:22,290
Delicious?

473
00:14:22,290 --> 00:14:23,040
It is.

474
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:30,580
(Behind-the-Scenes 10)

475
00:14:30,620 --> 00:14:31,920
(Behind-the-Scenes: Signal House)

476
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:33,310
There's a Heart's Answer here.

477
00:14:33,480 --> 00:14:35,110
Let me borrow this.

478
00:14:36,040 --> 00:14:38,190
How do we use this?

479
00:14:38,940 --> 00:14:40,140
(Curious)

480
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:41,950
Why don't you give it a try?

481
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,110
I want to ask

482
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:46,070
(Wu Siying asks)
if the guy I'm looking for will appear.

483
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,190
In Signal House.

484
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,620
Will he appear?

485
00:14:48,620 --> 00:14:49,500
(Will he appear?)

486
00:14:50,140 --> 00:14:51,500
(Looking from the side)

487
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:52,390
What does this mean?

488
00:14:52,400 --> 00:14:53,070
This...

489
00:14:53,080 --> 00:14:53,910
(Heart's Answer)
You don't need

490
00:14:53,920 --> 00:14:54,950
to complete a job for two people.

491
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,230
It means he'll appear.

492
00:14:56,400 --> 00:14:57,360
Can I understand it like that?

493
00:14:57,360 --> 00:14:58,170
I think so.

494
00:14:58,560 --> 00:14:59,510
You can try this.

495
00:14:59,520 --> 00:15:00,670
I should ask a question too.

496
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:03,700
(Thinking)

497
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:04,990
I'll ask the same question.

498
00:15:04,990 --> 00:15:05,440
Go ahead.

499
00:15:05,920 --> 00:15:07,310
(Chen Hewen asks)
After Signal House,

500
00:15:07,320 --> 00:15:08,870
will I meet the one I'm looking for?

501
00:15:09,950 --> 00:15:10,750
This one.

502
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:14,110
What does this mean?

503
00:15:14,640 --> 00:15:16,350
(Heart's Answer)
Be an outsider occasionally.

504
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:20,470
(Panics)
Let's put the book back, shall we?

505
00:15:24,040 --> 00:15:24,780
Hello.

506
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:25,840
Hi.

507
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:26,340
Xilun.

508
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:28,910
Did you see "Heart's Answer"?

509
00:15:30,040 --> 00:15:30,430
Not yet.

510
00:15:30,440 --> 00:15:31,670
I only saw the cover.

511
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:32,990
Think of a question.

512
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,950
Will I

513
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:37,790
(Zhao Xilun asks)
find love here?

514
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:38,510
Alright.

515
00:15:38,600 --> 00:15:39,670
Then I'll just flip open a page?

516
00:15:39,670 --> 00:15:40,260
Flip open a page.

517
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,630
Any page.

518
00:15:44,680 --> 00:15:45,800
Don't love someone who...

519
00:15:49,650 --> 00:15:50,590
(Heart's Answer)
Don't love someone

520
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:51,950
who makes you feel ordinary.

521
00:15:51,950 --> 00:15:52,390
No.

522
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,190
I'm done.

523
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:53,780
This book.

524
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:54,280
Forget it.

525
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:55,500
(Fleeing)

526
00:15:56,240 --> 00:15:57,030
Si,

527
00:15:57,600 --> 00:15:58,710
do you know?

528
00:15:59,170 --> 00:16:01,350
He was checking out
the "Heart's Answer".

529
00:16:01,890 --> 00:16:03,630
And he asked a question,

530
00:16:03,640 --> 00:16:05,350
"Will I find love here?"

531
00:16:05,360 --> 00:16:06,530
What was the answer again?

532
00:16:06,530 --> 00:16:07,150
Don't love someone

533
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:08,710
who makes you feel ordinary.

534
00:16:10,520 --> 00:16:12,270
Why are our answers like that?

535
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:17,260
(Behind-the-Scenes 11)

536
00:16:17,340 --> 00:16:19,420
(Behind-the-Scenes)

537
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:21,150
What's special about Pisces?

538
00:16:24,120 --> 00:16:26,070
Probably a little more...

539
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,630
Thoughtful.

540
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:33,220
Quite imaginative.

541
00:16:33,220 --> 00:16:34,620
(Imaginative)

542
00:16:36,940 --> 00:16:37,540
(Glances)

543
00:16:37,560 --> 00:16:40,150
I don't know much about signs.

544
00:16:41,370 --> 00:16:42,950
Same for MBTI too.

545
00:16:44,450 --> 00:16:45,950
I don't know MBTI either.

546
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:47,090
(Scratches head)
I'm done.

547
00:16:47,090 --> 00:16:47,790
Finished.

548
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:49,700
(Glances)

549
00:16:49,720 --> 00:16:52,660
(Comforts)
Shows you take your work seriously.

550
00:16:53,560 --> 00:16:55,550
I did work a lot before,

551
00:16:56,800 --> 00:16:58,110
but I feel like that's about to change.

552
00:17:00,560 --> 00:17:03,270
Life and love are both important.

553
00:17:08,880 --> 00:17:10,470
Do you usually go to concerts?

554
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:12,030
Yes.

555
00:17:12,290 --> 00:17:14,550
I work in live shows a lot.

556
00:17:17,070 --> 00:17:20,180
We were in Nanjing
or somewhere there the other day.

557
00:17:20,280 --> 00:17:22,070
We were done with sound check,

558
00:17:22,070 --> 00:17:25,440
but the weather forecast said
the next day...

559
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,640
That it would rain.

560
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:27,120
Yes.

561
00:17:28,400 --> 00:17:29,310
There was going to be a typhoon.

562
00:17:30,300 --> 00:17:31,980
(Listening intently)

563
00:17:32,840 --> 00:17:35,670
So at two in the morning,

564
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:39,190
we suddenly decided to leave.

565
00:17:39,920 --> 00:17:41,950
We got a cab to the airport

566
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:42,870
and flew to Haikou for a concert.

567
00:17:45,200 --> 00:17:46,630
You guys are such Judging types.

568
00:17:47,790 --> 00:17:49,130
Shouldn't it be the Perceiving type?

569
00:17:50,320 --> 00:17:51,030
Perceiving types are those

570
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:53,150
who don't plan.

571
00:17:53,720 --> 00:17:54,430
Yeah.

572
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:55,630
We didn't make a plan.

573
00:17:56,480 --> 00:17:57,550
Judging types are those

574
00:17:57,560 --> 00:17:59,230
who can immediately

575
00:17:59,230 --> 00:18:00,340
make changes

576
00:18:00,340 --> 00:18:01,300
to plans.

577
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,990
I think during work,

578
00:18:05,170 --> 00:18:06,680
I'm a Judging type.

579
00:18:07,560 --> 00:18:09,030
Your work requires the Judging type.

580
00:18:09,040 --> 00:18:09,670
Well.

581
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,750
If I'm at work,
I'd become the Judging type.

582
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:16,630
But I think

583
